# Keep the build context small, and — more importantly — correct.

# --- Installed dependencies (reinstalled inside the image) ---
# Copying the host's node_modules in would drag macOS binaries into a Linux
# image, and the pnpm symlink farm would be rebuilt anyway.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

# --- Build output (regenerated inside the image) ---
**/.next
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Environment files: must never reach an image ---
# packages/db/seed.ts loads .env with process.loadEnvFile, which OVERRIDES real
# environment variables. A stray .env in the image would therefore beat the
# container's DATABASE_URL and point seeding at the wrong database host.
# `.env.docker` is read by Compose from the host via --env-file, never copied.
.env
.env.*

# --- VCS / editor / OS noise ---
.git
.gitignore
**/.DS_Store
*.log

# --- Host-side orchestration (not needed inside an image) ---
docker-compose*.yml
Makefile
README.md
